{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1456251-aberrant-examples-and-what-darkstar-novas-would-be-like","id":1456251,"title":"[Aberrant] Examples and what darkstar novas would be like","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: Aberrant"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-08-06T10:50:59-07:00","id":1456251,"title":"[Aberrant] Examples and what darkstar novas would be like","content":"I've just been watching the movie Lucy and I had a thought that this is a good example of what a darkstar nova could do and be like.<br /> <br /> Some of the feats she does are awesome and it at how a good example of some of the mega attributes and mega edges.<br /> <br /> Can anyone else think of good examples of darkstar novas or feats you think they could do.<br /> <br /> If I could erupt on n day as Darkstar nova I would probably use my abilities to gain wealth and live a hedonistic lifestyle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26058-aeonstorm","name":"Aeonstorm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-06T14:50:35-07:00","id":1456267,"title":"","content":"Hannibal Lecter is a great example of this. He's brilliant to the point of absurdity, persuasive to the point of talking someone into committing suicide, and exceptionally physically dangerous. His attitude is also on-point for a Dark Star Nova in the Teragen (okay, most Terats don't go quite that far, but the attitude is more different in degree than in kind).<br /> <br /> Any action movie protagonist, especially something on the higher-powered end is probably Dark Star appropriate (probably without Mega-Intellect or Mega-Manipulation, though there are exceptions there, but very likely to have literally all the rest at low levels).<br /> <br /> 'Normal human' superheroes are also usually good fodder for this (Black Widow in the MCU, for example, can easily be argued to have Mega-Attributes in literally everything, as can Batman in, well, everything), as are 'low end' superhumans of other sorts (Captain America has most of the Mega-Attributes, and few higher than 2 or so).<br /> <br /> A lot of these could also be represented by Talents as well, but Dark Stars blur that line somewhat intentionally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26949-deadmanwalking","user":"Deadmanwalking","date":". 08-06-2021, 05:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26949-deadmanwalking","name":"Deadmanwalking","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-06T19:19:10-07:00","id":1456272,"title":"","content":"Don't forget that Novas can have more than Powers and Mega-Attributes; they can spend their points on mundane Attribute dots and Paths as well. This gives them significantly bigger dice pools without adding any blatantly superhuman abilities.<br /> <br /> Consider an example Nova who sticks one dot into Mega-Intellect to justify being super smart enough to casually buy up all their Paths at character creation, then dump everything else into raising all their base Attributes to the three to five range. Most of their dice pools before adding equipment or specialty bonuses are going to be in the six to eight range, and they roll versus a TN of 7. They are astonishingly competent at almost everything by mundane standards.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-07T04:32:04-07:00","id":1456293,"title":"","content":"Penguin in Batman comics could be a good example. He looks like a dumpy little guy, there's a reason Danny Devito played Penguin in a movie. But he's a dangerous combatant and he's a genius string-puller who can destroy people's lives on a whim.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-07T06:09:38-07:00","id":1456300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deadmanwalking</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1456251-aberrant-examples-and-what-darkstar-novas-would-be-like?p=1456267#post1456267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hannibal Lecter is a great example of this. He's brilliant to the point of absurdity, persuasive to the point of talking someone into committing suicide, and exceptionally physically dangerous. His attitude is also on-point for a Dark Star Nova in the Teragen (okay, most Terats don't go quite that far, but the attitude is more different in degree than in kind).<br /> <br /> Any action movie protagonist, especially something on the higher-powered end is probably Dark Star appropriate (probably without Mega-Intellect or Mega-Manipulation, though there are exceptions there, but very likely to have literally all the rest at low levels).<br /> <br /> 'Normal human' superheroes are also usually good fodder for this (Black Widow in the MCU, for example, can easily be argued to have Mega-Attributes in literally everything, as can Batman in, well, everything), as are 'low end' superhumans of other sorts (Captain America has most of the Mega-Attributes, and few higher than 2 or so).<br /> <br /> A lot of these could also be represented by Talents as well, but Dark Stars blur that line somewhat intentionally.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think Hannibal Lector is a great example. I also agree with Captain America and Black Widow. Batman and action movie protagonists would fall more under Talents. Here's my argument: the difference between a Dark Star and a Talent is competence vs luck and plot manipulation. The way the henchmen always miss in action movies? Plot manipulation. Batman having a contingency and prep for everything at all times? Plot manipulation. What about Batman's competence? True he's good at everything, but it's how he's good at everything. He seems to be so unbelievably competent that he almost acquires skills as the story calls for it. This seems more like a Talent's gifts. <br /> <br /> Compare this to Black Widow. She is extremely skilled, using that 150 xp to be dumped into skills with maybe a point dumped into Mega-Stamina (I think she has boosted healing in the comics?) and Mega-Cunning. Her skills however never seem to break the break the plot the way Bruce Wayne or an action movie protagonist does.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26906-jeffreybezos","name":"JeffreyBezos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-07T06:11:57-07:00","id":1456301,"title":"","content":"Lex Luthor. XP goes to Paths, Wealth, Intellect and the like. Kingpin (similar rationale, and probably also has Mega-Stamina 1 in some incarnations).<br /> <br /> any MCU &quot;Super-Soldier Serum&quot; user.<br /> <br /> Hawkeye &amp; Green Arrow.<br /> <br /> any &quot;uber martial artist without any superpowers&quot; in comics and the like (Marvel TV Series' Davos, sans Iron Fist).<br /> <br /> The Riddler (Mega-Intellect).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1001-timecrafter","name":"Timecrafter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1001_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-07T15:09:58-07:00","id":1456315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JeffreyBezos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1456251-aberrant-examples-and-what-darkstar-novas-would-be-like?p=1456300#post1456300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Hannibal Lector is a great example. I also agree with Captain America and Black Widow. Batman and action movie protagonists would fall more under Talents. Here's my argument: the difference between a Dark Star and a Talent is competence vs luck and plot manipulation. The way the henchmen always miss in action movies? Plot manipulation. Batman having a contingency and prep for everything at all times? Plot manipulation. What about Batman's competence? True he's good at everything, but it's how he's good at everything. He seems to be so unbelievably competent that he almost acquires skills as the story calls for it. This seems more like a Talent's gifts.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> I did say the line was blurry between the two. For Batman specifically 'having a plan for that' is absolutely plot manipulation...but it's precisely the kind of plot manipulation that the Foresight Mega-Edge allows, and 'skills as needed' sounds a lot like Instant Expert to me. Batman can certainly also be made as a Talent, but you can build a character with equivalent abilities as a Dark Star Nova pretty readily. For action movie protagonists, it depends on the action movie. There's a reason that I specified the ones on the higher powered end. John McClane is definitely a Talent, but The Bride in Kill Bill is probably better built as a Nova.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JeffreyBezos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1456251-aberrant-examples-and-what-darkstar-novas-would-be-like?p=1456300#post1456300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Compare this to Black Widow. She is extremely skilled, using that 150 xp to be dumped into skills with maybe a point dumped into Mega-Stamina (I think she has boosted healing in the comics?) and Mega-Cunning. Her skills however never seem to break the break the plot the way Bruce Wayne or an action movie protagonist does.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the MCU, at least, I'd probably give her dots in almost every Mega-Attribute (even one in Mega-Might...she's notably stronger than a woman her size is likely to be). She successfully tricks Loki, is brilliant (if not on, say, Tony Stark's level), and routinely pulls off some acrobatic stuff that is somewhere between unlikely and impossible (that's Mega-Manipulation, low Mega-Intellect, and heaps of Mega-Dexterity right there).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26949-deadmanwalking","name":"Deadmanwalking","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-07T22:09:34-07:00","id":1456334,"title":"","content":"Batman is tricky just because there have been so many ways he has been depicted. In the older movies and animated series I would put him as a Talent for sure. The Arkham games I could see either but would peg him as Nova though a high level Talent is plausible. Comics? Nova with at least a dot in every Mega-Attribute full stop.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4178-stanlemon","name":"stanlemon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-08T03:29:23-07:00","id":1456342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>stanlemon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1456251-aberrant-examples-and-what-darkstar-novas-would-be-like?p=1456334#post1456334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Batman is tricky just because there have been so many ways he has been depicted. In the older movies and animated series I would put him as a Talent for sure. The Arkham games I could see either but would peg him as Nova though a high level Talent is plausible. Comics? Nova with at least a dot in every Mega-Attribute full stop.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually think that, with The Bigger They Are particularly as applied to mental and social contests, this system can do a fair job of even comic level Batman as a Talent, but the Mega-Attribute and Edge version is probably still better at reflecting that. I mean, almost all Batman's 'plot manipulation' takes the form of prior plans, and a Mega-Intellect and Mega-Cunning focused Nova actually winds up with more 'Inspiration' to use for that than Talents do, generally speaking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26949-deadmanwalking","name":"Deadmanwalking","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-08T05:36:32-07:00","id":1456346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deadmanwalking</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1456251-aberrant-examples-and-what-darkstar-novas-would-be-like?p=1456315#post1456315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I did say the line was blurry between the two. For Batman specifically 'having a plan for that' is absolutely plot manipulation...but it's precisely the kind of plot manipulation that the Foresight Mega-Edge allows, and 'skills as needed' sounds a lot like Instant Expert to me. Batman can certainly also be made as a Talent, but you can build a character with equivalent abilities as a Dark Star Nova pretty readily. For action movie protagonists, it depends on the action movie. There's a reason that I specified the ones on the higher powered end. John McClane is definitely a Talent, but The Bride in Kill Bill is probably better built as a Nova.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh wow, I completely missed Foresight. That's a huge gamechanger. I'd say that's the nail in the coffin to my argument, but now I'm almost tackling this from the other direction. It does seem you can model MCU mortal characters extremely effectively as Darkstars. So where do Talents come in?<br /> <br /> Originally I assumed characters like Winter Soldier and Captain America to be Darkstars, Hawkeye and Black Widow to Talents, and secondary characters like Agent Coulson to be skilled Baselines. Maybe the scale is upped a bit. Agent Coulson level characters are actually the Talents. Civilians and bystanders are the baselines, and all the main characters that take the spotlight are Novas?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26906,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26906-jeffreybezos","user":"JeffreyBezos","date":". 08-08-2021, 08:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26906-jeffreybezos","name":"JeffreyBezos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-08T05:47:05-07:00","id":1456347,"title":"","content":"By the way. Remembering when they introduced Harley Quinn into the comics (she started as Joker's TV sidekick, and he did kick her) Poison Ivy gave Harley healing potions and more. <br /> <br /> Harley would be a Darkstar Nova type. She wouldn't have Physical Mega attributes, but a small woman like Harley having the strength of a linebacker and the resilience of an ox, combined with the agility of an Olympic level gymnast, would be impressive. Add to that Harley is a PHd holder, a clinical psychologist. <br /> <br /> Harley would make an excellent Darkstar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-08T07:34:41-07:00","id":1456349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JeffreyBezos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1456251-aberrant-examples-and-what-darkstar-novas-would-be-like?p=1456346#post1456346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Oh wow, I completely missed Foresight. That's a huge gamechanger. I'd say that's the nail in the coffin to my argument, but now I'm almost tackling this from the other direction. It does seem you can model MCU mortal characters extremely effectively as Darkstars. So where do Talents come in?</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Originally I assumed characters like Winter Soldier and Captain America to be Darkstars, Hawkeye and Black Widow to Talents, and secondary characters like Agent Coulson to be skilled Baselines. Maybe the scale is upped a bit. Agent Coulson level characters are actually the Talents. Civilians and bystanders are the baselines, and all the main characters that take the spotlight are Novas?</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Coulson would definitely be a Talent, yeah. I could see Nick Fury as sort of a 'high end' for Talents in the MCU, he's very competent but in direct confrontations with real supers he's not quite on par. People more central than that are probably best built as Novas of one sort or another.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1456251-aberrant-examples-and-what-darkstar-novas-would-be-like?p=1456347#post1456347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By the way. Remembering when they introduced Harley Quinn into the comics (she started as Joker's TV sidekick, and he did kick her) Poison Ivy gave Harley healing potions and more.<br /> <br /> Harley would be a Darkstar Nova type. She wouldn't have Physical Mega attributes, but a small woman like Harley having the strength of a linebacker and the resilience of an ox, combined with the agility of an Olympic level gymnast, would be impressive. Add to that Harley is a PHd holder, a clinical psychologist.<br /> <br /> Harley would make an excellent Darkstar.</div> </div> </div> </div>If Batman is a Dark Star Nova the Joker almost certainly is as well (some of his other villains might just be Talents, in some cases with The Bigger They Are, but the Joker matches Batman more directly, in particular demonstrating Mega-Social stuff at a pretty high level, IMO), and that being the case Harley being one as well is probably needed, and her physical abilities (including, in Aberrant terms, probably Mega-Cunning for initiative and senses and Mega-Resolve for pain tolerance) probably qualify as superhuman in most continuities by this point, making doing so pretty easy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26949-deadmanwalking","name":"Deadmanwalking","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-08T11:39:45-07:00","id":1456357,"title":"","content":"Tattletale from &quot;Worm&quot;. She basically has only Mega-Cunning and its associated Mega-Edges as powers. You can model her pretty well that way. In &quot;Worm&quot;, Taylor (Skitter) notes that Lisa (Tattletale) could have been a horrifyingly effective cult leader if she had gone that route.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26999,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26999-rhiannon-vashti","user":"Rhiannon Vashti","date":". 08-08-2021, 03:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26999-rhiannon-vashti","name":"Rhiannon Vashti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26999_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-08T11:42:14-07:00","id":1456360,"title":"","content":"Some of the characters from the Watchmen movie might be darkstars too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-08T16:12:06-07:00","id":1456376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rhiannon Vashti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1456251-aberrant-examples-and-what-darkstar-novas-would-be-like?p=1456357#post1456357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tattletale from &quot;Worm&quot;. She basically has only Mega-Cunning and its associated Mega-Edges as powers. You can model her pretty well that way. In &quot;Worm&quot;, Taylor (Skitter) notes that Lisa (Tattletale) could have been a horrifyingly effective cult leader if she had gone that route.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tattletale's power would also include Mega-Manipulation, IMO, she regularly uses the info she gets for social engineering. A bit of Mega-Intellect and Mega-Composure probably also make sense, But yes, she's all Mega-Attributes and Edges with not a power in sight. Her tricks might be a little too overtly supernatural to be a true Dark Star, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26949-deadmanwalking","name":"Deadmanwalking","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-08T18:27:02-07:00","id":1456383,"title":"","content":"Talent vs. Darkstar is very much like like Daredevil vs. Stalwart. How do you decide if your Adventure-era character should be a daredevil or a stalwart? (Or a mesmerist, for that matter.) And can that decision process be applied to the Aberrant era?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-08T22:49:43-07:00","id":1456391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JeffreyBezos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1456251-aberrant-examples-and-what-darkstar-novas-would-be-like?p=1456346#post1456346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe the scale is upped a bit. Agent Coulson level characters are actually the Talents. Civilians and bystanders are the baselines, and all the main characters that take the spotlight are Novas?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's kind of where I put things, though &quot;bystanders&quot; for me include Shield agents, soldiers, and the like. Black Widow &amp; Hawkeye are definitely Talents. Same with Fury. Coulson kind of has to be given everything he's gone through (and coming back from the dead &amp; all). Cap America could be a Superior (even sorta matches the origin) but if you're working with only Core &amp; Aberrant then Dark Star works too. Same goes for Black Panther.<br /> <br /> Iron Man comes across as a Q-Tech Aberrant with Mega-Intelligence and a whole lotta points invested in his armour. Pretty much everyone else (at the Avengers level) are Aberrant or higher.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26905-eternl-knight","name":"Eternl Knight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26905_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-09T00:17:47-07:00","id":1456394,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deadmanwalking</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1456251-aberrant-examples-and-what-darkstar-novas-would-be-like?p=1456376#post1456376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Tattletale's power would also include Mega-Manipulation, IMO, she regularly uses the info she gets for social engineering. A bit of Mega-Intellect and Mega-Composure probably also make sense, But yes, she's all Mega-Attributes and Edges with not a power in sight. Her tricks might be a little too overtly supernatural to be a true Dark Star, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suspect that Tattletale has just regular Manipulation. Her leadership powers aren't the greatest and by the time of &quot;Ward&quot;, the Undersiders were in the process of fragmenting into four different factions. However, her Mega-Cunning does provide her with excellent material to mess with people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26999-rhiannon-vashti","name":"Rhiannon Vashti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26999_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-09T05:06:31-07:00","id":1456416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rhiannon Vashti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1456251-aberrant-examples-and-what-darkstar-novas-would-be-like?p=1456394#post1456394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suspect that Tattletale has just regular Manipulation. Her leadership powers aren't the greatest and by the time of &quot;Ward&quot;, the Undersiders were in the process of fragmenting into four different factions. However, her Mega-Cunning does provide her with excellent material to mess with people.</div> </div> </div> </div>Manipulation (and thus Mega-Manipulation) doesn't necessarily make you likable, exactly, just good at pushing people's buttons (to quote the Aberrant book, Mega Presence can 'inspire fanatical devotion' but Mega-Manipulation cannot do that, but can instead 'make people dance to their tune without even knowing they're doing it'), which seems appropriate to Tattletale (particularly in combination with mediocre Presence). I would probably only give her a point or so of it, mind you (to go with about the same in Mega-Intellect and much higher Mega-Cunning).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26949-deadmanwalking","name":"Deadmanwalking","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-09T07:57:47-07:00","id":1456430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1456251-aberrant-examples-and-what-darkstar-novas-would-be-like?p=1456383#post1456383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Talent vs. Darkstar is very much like like Daredevil vs. Stalwart. How do you decide if your Adventure-era character should be a daredevil or a stalwart? (Or a mesmerist, for that matter.) And can that decision process be applied to the Aberrant era?</div> </div> </div> </div>I haven't read through the Adventure manuscripts too terribly in depth, but do Stalwarts get an xp boost? The 150 bonus xp and boost to tier 7 seems a pretty big power difference. That boost could be put towards skills and one dot of mega-attribute to really show an Avengers level mortal like Hawkeye much more than what a talent offers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eternl Knight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1456251-aberrant-examples-and-what-darkstar-novas-would-be-like?p=1456391#post1456391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's kind of where I put things, though &quot;bystanders&quot; for me include Shield agents, soldiers, and the like. Black Widow &amp; Hawkeye are definitely Talents. Same with Fury. Coulson kind of has to be given everything he's gone through (and coming back from the dead &amp; all). Cap America could be a Superior (even sorta matches the origin) but if you're working with only Core &amp; Aberrant then Dark Star works too. Same goes for Black Panther.<br /> <br /> Iron Man comes across as a Q-Tech Aberrant with Mega-Intelligence and a whole lotta points invested in his armour. Pretty much everyone else (at the Avengers level) are Aberrant or higher.</div> </div> </div> </div>Here's where I think it gets tricky. While theme wise it seems easy to say high level mortals are talents, I think there's a few game changers that rule them out. Foresight mega-edge that allows Novas to dramatically edit really takes away the main advantage of playing Talents. I'm not just talking min-maxing here to create an optimal character. Foresight also comes into playstyle differences. If we can have Novas that can dramatically edit, they can have the plot armor of Talents while still having access to Q-tech while also hitting a target number of 7: the competence you would expect to come from an elite agent. <br /> <br /> Now, if we have competent characters that lag a bit behind the rest of the crew, that makes sense. Fury is lucky and contribute to the story, he's a Talent. Black Widow? She's front and center of an alien invasion while fighting super villains- Dark Star.<br /> <br /> I think it's that power difference and the role you want your character to tell in the story that separates the Dark Star from the Talent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26906,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26906-jeffreybezos","user":"JeffreyBezos","date":". 08-09-2021, 11:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26906-jeffreybezos","name":"JeffreyBezos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-09T09:32:55-07:00","id":1456438,"title":"","content":"You can have a Nova that spent all the 150 XP in skills, attributes and other mundane things, what would make them the ultimate DarkStar, not even themselves understanding or seeing themselves as Novas, they would still pop in a quantum detector, and would be able to use Qtech (not much, too little juice to power them).<br /> <br /> But that is the amazing part of what is a Nova and what is not, from the general population understanding, a Talent with high inspiration can be seen as a Nova for ALL that luck, or all the amazing skills they show even with no proper power. Same for a Psiad, they have powers so they must be a Nova, nobody care if they don\u2019t show in quantum detectors, as far as we know popping in quantum detectors may just mean they can use their powers while dormant or that they have a stealth power that protect them from being detected, or even they have a weird signature that is out of tune with the detector. Using that criteria, you can easily recreate all the Avengers and even more as Novas. The system is even more flexible, you can create Dr Strange, Goku, Lex Luthor, even Machine Man as Novas, but they are not, none of them are.<br /> <br /> So, you can play a game of Aberrant where everyone is a Nova, no matter what is the character theme, in this game Batman is a Nova, same way as Superman. Or you can have a game where Supers are Novas and non supers are Talents. It\u2019s a matter of what you feel would be appropriate.<br /> <br /> There is one single problem in the first option, if you are a Nova, you pop in quantum detectors, so anyone can differentiate a Nova from a baseline (you can have novas that don\u2019t show in the quantum detector, but not baselines that show). In universe, Black Widow, Hawkeye, Batman, Green Arrow, Kingpin, etc etc are not Supers, they don\u2019t have powers, they are not mutant, they are not aliens, they have no source of powers, they are humans very well trained, very competent and prepared to all situations, in other words, they are Talents.<br /> <br /> But taking the same criteria, Tony Stark is human, not generally human, completely human, he is a genius, capable of inventing technology that others can\u2019t, but his tech is not reality bending, it\u2019s just absurdly advanced. His armor is not powered by him, in the best description he was powered by the same source as the armor. His inventions have their own source of power (it\u2019s the main reason why it\u2019s so hard to replicate his tech, it consumes too much energy and is still compact), so Rescue, Warmachine and many others have used some of his armors with no difficulties. You can say those armors are Nova tech versions, but they are just old designs or adaptations of old designs.<br /> <br /> In truth, anovas and Talrnts are setting specifics, that can be expanded to fit other concepts, but not entirely, Superman can be portraited as a Nova in TC, but is he quantum powered or is it a very specific set of Psionic powers? If you read the old description of the X-men powers they are ALL Psionic powers somehow, Colossus have a Psionic capacity of turning his flesh into organic metal, Cyclops blast is made of Psionic energy, etc. Does it make them Psiads? Not really, they fit bette as Novas.<br /> <br /> My preference is, if you want to play a human play as a Talent, if not play as a Nova. But I want to play as a Psiad! Sure, you can, there are a few hundred of them in Earth, so why not. Same apply to all NPCs. Being a Nova have some impacts in setting, even if you are a DarkStar, and so it is important to pick wisely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-09T11:32:55-07:00","id":1456442,"title":"","content":"Note that Foresight is specifically limited to Dramatic Editing that represents retroactively having planned ahead; that's why it's tied to Mega-Intellect and Mega-Cunning. Talent Dramatic Editing has no such restriction; they can go with any character concept and attribute spread and still get full access to Dramatic Editing. In order for a Nova with Foresight to keep up with a Talent on Dramatic Editing beyond starting characters, the Nova always needs literally inhuman levels of Mega-Intellect and/or Mega-Cunning: Talents always start with a minimum Inspiration of 3 (the one point that all Talents automatically have, plus two or three more points from their Facets), meaning that a Nova with Foresight would need at least one of Mega-Intellect or Mega-Cunning to be at least two \u2014 which makes it somewhat difficult to consider that Nova to be a Darkstar. And this problem only intensifies the more the Talent's Facets are raised. And Foresight isn't conceptually appropriate to many Mega-Intellect/Mega-Cunning Novas, either: Tony Stark is very much a Mega-Intellect Nova, possibly with as many as five dots in it; but he's not much on the \u201cplanning ahead\u201d thing, and there's no way I'd give him Foresight. <br /> <br /> And if it's just a matter of experience that puts the Talent at a disadvantage, just give the Talent more experience. There's precedent for that, in that the likes of Batman and Black Widow tend to have undergone some form of intensive training to get to the level they're at. Meanwhile, don't forget that Talents can do things with their Inspiration that Novas can't (easily) do: a Talent can increase the Intensity Scale of any action just by spending a point of Inspiration; a Nova needs to acquire a point of Flux to do the equivalent, with all the hassles that come with that; <i>and</i> he has to find some way to justify it through a Nova trait: Novas can't Max Out Skills or Edges.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-09T13:01:16-07:00","id":1456451,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1456251-aberrant-examples-and-what-darkstar-novas-would-be-like?p=1456442#post1456442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Note that Foresight is specifically limited to Dramatic Editing that represents retroactively having planned ahead; that's why it's tied to Mega-Intellect and Mega-Cunning. Talent Dramatic Editing has no such restriction; they can go with any character concept and attribute spread and still get full access to Dramatic Editing.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> This is a super good point to keep in mind, though it can be difficult to tell the difference from the outside (Violet 'Tank' Cho is listed with probability manipulation powers in the Aberrant book...she almost certainly has Foresight to represent a good part of that). There's a reason that I brought this up specifically in regards to Batman, as he's a classic example of a character who, given Inspiration, basically never uses it for anything other than 'retroactively planned ahead for this', rather than Talents in general. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1456251-aberrant-examples-and-what-darkstar-novas-would-be-like?p=1456442#post1456442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In order for a Nova with Foresight to keep up with a Talent on Dramatic Editing beyond starting characters, the Nova always needs literally inhuman levels of Mega-Intellect and/or Mega-Cunning: Talents always start with a minimum Inspiration of 3 (the one point that all Talents automatically have, plus two or three more points from their Facets), meaning that a Nova with Foresight would need at least one of Mega-Intellect or Mega-Cunning to be at least two \u2014 which makes it somewhat difficult to consider that Nova to be a Darkstar. And this problem only intensifies the more the Talent's Facets are raised.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> Mega-Intellect and in particular Mega-Cunning are really easy Mega-Attributes to conceal if you have a mind to. So it depends on how you define a Dark Star, really. Is the line 'they themselves might not realize they're a Nova' or is it 'outside observers would have trouble realizing they're a Nova'? Because yeah, if it's the former, high Mega-Cunning or Mega-Intellect will make you 'no longer a Dark Star' pretty rapidly, but if it's the latter (where I'd argue a Nova version of Batman lives, just as one example), then you can probably reach as high as you'd like in Mega-Cunning and Mega-Composure, and likely at least 2 levels in most of the other Mega-Attributes (barring Mega-Presence and Mega-Might) before people start getting really suspicious as long as you're careful how and when you use them. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1456251-aberrant-examples-and-what-darkstar-novas-would-be-like?p=1456442#post1456442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And Foresight isn't conceptually appropriate to many Mega-Intellect/Mega-Cunning Novas, either: Tony Stark is very much a Mega-Intellect Nova, possibly with as many as five dots in it; but he's not much on the \u201cplanning ahead\u201d thing, and there's no way I'd give him Foresight.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> This is certainly true. It's far from universally applicable.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1456251-aberrant-examples-and-what-darkstar-novas-would-be-like?p=1456442#post1456442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And if it's just a matter of experience that puts the Talent at a disadvantage, just give the Talent more experience. There's precedent for that, in that the likes of Batman and Black Widow tend to have undergone some form of intensive training to get to the level they're at. Meanwhile, don't forget that Talents can do things with their Inspiration that Novas can't (easily) do: a Talent can increase the Intensity Scale of any action just by spending a point of Inspiration; a Nova needs to acquire a point of Flux to do the equivalent, with all the hassles that come with that; <i>and</i> he has to find some way to justify it through a Nova trait: Novas can't Max Out Skills or Edges.</div> </div> </div> </div>My personal House Rule in terms of power level is that Talents and Psiads (or, theoretically, Psions) intended to play at the same power level as Novas receive 30 xp less than Novas get from their template (so 120 xp if using standard 150 xp Novas) on top of the other stuff they get at character creation. That narrows the gap quite a bit, but Novas still wind up more generally powerful, IMO.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26949-deadmanwalking","name":"Deadmanwalking","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-09T14:23:35-07:00","id":1456455,"title":"","content":"Batman does more than just planning ahead. Batman is always using Extreme Effort, Plot Armor, and for sure have more than a few combat gifts to fight almost any kind of adversary.<br /> <br /> From an in universe point of view, even if you have a outsider view, like when we read comics, Dramatic Editing does not exist, because we don\u2019t know the difference between what the GM narrated and what the Player did, plan ahead is the easiest to catch, as it\u2019s impossible anyone can keep track of so many plans, but Batman Player for sure added some stuff to the setting that we don\u2019t know\u2026<br /> <br /> Talents are absolutely flexible and can gain scale on ANY action, what is not something easy, plus sometimes can do that with momentum instead of inspiration (skill tricks). Psions and Psiads are also versatile (Psiads more than psions), their powers are more flexible than Nova powers, a few dots and you gain a nice set of powers instead of a single very powerful power. The only chance novas have to reach a fraction of the flexibility is with power stunts.<br /> <br /> My counting for extra XP to any other splat is 50-60XP to Talents and Psiads (or Psions that don\u2019t work as a group too), 40-50XP to Psions (that have more Psions to work with) and 30-40XP to Superiors. All the other splats evolve faster than Novas, Superiors specially, while not capable of reach the same level of power Novas can reach, they all can be useful and playable side by side with Novas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-09T18:02:53-07:00","id":1456480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deadmanwalking</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1456251-aberrant-examples-and-what-darkstar-novas-would-be-like?p=1456451#post1456451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is a super good point to keep in mind, though it can be difficult to tell the difference from the outside (Violet 'Tank' Cho is listed with probability manipulation powers in the Aberrant book...she almost certainly has Foresight to represent a good part of that). There's a reason that I brought this up specifically in regards to Batman, as he's a classic example of a character who, given Inspiration, basically never uses it for anything other than 'retroactively planned ahead for this', rather than Talents in general.<br /> <br /> Mega-Intellect and in particular Mega-Cunning are really easy Mega-Attributes to conceal if you have a mind to. So it depends on how you define a Dark Star, really. Is the line 'they themselves might not realize they're a Nova' or is it 'outside observers would have trouble realizing they're a Nova'? Because yeah, if it's the former, high Mega-Cunning or Mega-Intellect will make you 'no longer a Dark Star' pretty rapidly, but if it's the latter (where I'd argue a Nova version of Batman lives, just as one example), then you can probably reach as high as you'd like in Mega-Cunning and Mega-Composure, and likely at least 2 levels in most of the other Mega-Attributes (barring Mega-Presence and Mega-Might) before people start getting really suspicious as long as you're careful how and when you use them.</div> </div> </div> </div>By that rationale, a Nova with Quantum Powers that make extensive use of the Subtle tag, or who simply make sure that no one sees them using their Quantum Powers (e.g., someone with Morph who never activates it while anyone is watching, or someone with Remote Perception who doesn't let on that she's spying on anyone) would be a dark star. I wouldn't go that far. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deadmanwalking</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1456251-aberrant-examples-and-what-darkstar-novas-would-be-like?p=1456451#post1456451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">And Foresight isn't conceptually appropriate to many Mega-Intellect/Mega-Cunning Novas, either: Tony Stark is very much a Mega-Intellect Nova, possibly with as many as five dots in it; but he's not much on the \u201cplanning ahead\u201d thing, and there's no way I'd give him Foresight.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is certainly true. It's far from universally applicable.</div> </div> </div> </div>But it's true more often than not. Hawkeye and Black Widow don't strike me as terribly sure to Foresight, either. Just because Foresight exists, that doesn't mean that it's any more common than any <i>other</i> Mega-Edge. Assuming that every Mega-Intellect/Mega-Cunning Nova has it is like assuming that every Talent has \u201cThe Bigger They Are\u201d. <br /> <br /> And even some concepts that <i>are</i> suited to Foresight could be better handled as experienced Talents: the Reflective Facet is very similar in feel to Foresight. I could easily see modeling Batman's \u201ccrazy prepared\u201d vibe with five dots of the Reflective Facet. I'd also give him at least three dots of the Destructive Facet, and possibly even a full five (Batman's very big on powering through on sheer grit), and a few dots in the Intuitive Facet (though of the three, that's where he's weakest). Oh, and \u201cThe Bigger They Are\u201d. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deadmanwalking</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1456251-aberrant-examples-and-what-darkstar-novas-would-be-like?p=1456451#post1456451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My personal House Rule in terms of power level is that Talents and Psiads (or, theoretically, Psions) intended to play at the same power level as Novas receive 30 xp less than Novas get from their template (so 120 xp if using standard 150 xp Novas) on top of the other stuff they get at character creation. That narrows the gap quite a bit, but Novas still wind up more generally powerful, IMO.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's more generous than I would be, surprisingly. <br /> <br /> While neither TC not the TC Adventure manuscript gives a table for experienced characters the way TC Aberrant does, TC \u00c6on does: Experienced characters get an extra 10 points, hardened veterans get 50, hardened veterans get 100, and \u201cProxies or exceptional Talents\u201d (their phrasing) get 150. Considering the phrasing on that last one, I take that chart (p.125) to apply to <i>everyone</i>, save only for Novas who have their own chart that overrides it. <br /> <br /> And yes, that does put non-Novas roughly a hundred experience points behind Novas. But as Mateus Luz says, they have their own benefits. If you're still concerned that they're too far behind, I could see tossing an extra, say, 50 experience their way on general principle; maybe even as much as 100. <br /> <br /> But I'm not sure that they need it. As Mateus Luz says, Talents and Psi-actives don't <i>need</i> as much experience, at least when leaning into their special powers: Gifts cost 4 or 5 xp; Modes cost 6, 8, or 10 xp (for Psions, psiad primaries, and psiad secondaries); Nova Traits mostly cost 12 xp (unless you're willing to take on Transcendence, which has its own price). Facets cost 10 xp; Psi costs 12/15 or 24/30; Quantum costs 16 or 32. And Talents arguably get more from their Facets than Novas get from their Quantum. <br /> <br /> And with all that in mind, I'd be perfectly happy insisting that a Nova <i>can't</i> spend all of the added xp they get on non-Nova traits. It's rarely an issue, because who in their right mind would play a Nova with no Nova Traits? But I could see insisting that at least 75 to 100 of those experience points should be spend on Nova Traits in one form or another, with the other 50 to 75 prioritizing Nova-related traits such as allegiance or Dormancy over Skills, Skill Tricks, or Edges that anyone can get. And anyone who <i>knows</i> the Nova before and after her Eruption will tend to think of whatever skills come from those points as a sort of Nova Trait, too \u2014 not because the skills can do anything particularly unusual (they can't), but because they came out of nowhere, and are <i>not</i> the result of training: the Nova Erupted, and suddenly could perform at a level that she couldn't before.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-09T18:51:45-07:00","id":1456486,"title":"","content":"maybe the answer is &quot;what Batman?&quot;. I can imagine some depictions as a Talent - don't underestimate Reflective and Destructive Facets. But I also can see in some depictions, in more &quot;high-powered&quot; media (or in those that he clearly is beyond human) that he could be a nova. Maybe this is why it's hard to pinpoint Batsie's &quot;to be or not to be&quot;. :-]","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1001-timecrafter","name":"Timecrafter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1001_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-09T19:07:47-07:00","id":1456488,"title":"","content":"I know of no portrayal of Batman where he's clearly beyond human. I know of a few where he's maxed out on Inspiration and loaded to the gills with both Gifts and Inspired Super-Science; but he's never <i>clearly</i> beyond human.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-09T21:23:16-07:00","id":1456495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1456251-aberrant-examples-and-what-darkstar-novas-would-be-like?p=1456455#post1456455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Batman does more than just planning ahead. Batman is always using Extreme Effort, Plot Armor, and for sure have more than a few combat gifts to fight almost any kind of adversary.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> If he's a Talent? Absolutely. If he's a Nova? He doesn't really need to use it for all that, having other traits to represent that sort of thing. IMO, Batman is easily made as either.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1456251-aberrant-examples-and-what-darkstar-novas-would-be-like?p=1456455#post1456455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From an in universe point of view, even if you have a outsider view, like when we read comics, Dramatic Editing does not exist, because we don\u2019t know the difference between what the GM narrated and what the Player did, plan ahead is the easiest to catch, as it\u2019s impossible anyone can keep track of so many plans, but Batman Player for sure added some stuff to the setting that we don\u2019t know\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> It's totally possible and Batman makes a fine Talent, but the only Dramatic Editing <i>conceptually necessary</i> for Batman as a character is covered by Foresight. He could have more, certainly, but is not required to, which allows for him to be made as a Nova in a way that someone whose luck is more unreasonable in other ways cannot be.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1456251-aberrant-examples-and-what-darkstar-novas-would-be-like?p=1456455#post1456455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Talents are absolutely flexible and can gain scale on ANY action, what is not something easy, plus sometimes can do that with momentum instead of inspiration (skill tricks). Psions and Psiads are also versatile (Psiads more than psions), their powers are more flexible than Nova powers, a few dots and you gain a nice set of powers instead of a single very powerful power. The only chance novas have to reach a fraction of the flexibility is with power stunts.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> Techniques go a long way to closing this disparity, IMO, especially with a particularly versatile power or two (I'm looking at you Transformation) thrown in.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1456251-aberrant-examples-and-what-darkstar-novas-would-be-like?p=1456455#post1456455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My counting for extra XP to any other splat is 50-60XP to Talents and Psiads (or Psions that don\u2019t work as a group too), 40-50XP to Psions (that have more Psions to work with) and 30-40XP to Superiors. All the other splats evolve faster than Novas, Superiors specially, while not capable of reach the same level of power Novas can reach, they all can be useful and playable side by side with Novas.</div> </div> </div> </div>Novas are also sitting at 160 xp extra due to their extra Attribute point. Well, as the discussion of my Polymath House Rule indicates, Novas wind up a bit more powerful on average in many games, so a bit of extra xp for others seems reasonable.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1456251-aberrant-examples-and-what-darkstar-novas-would-be-like?p=1456480#post1456480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By that rationale, a Nova with Quantum Powers that make extensive use of the Subtle tag, or who simply make sure that no one sees them using their Quantum Powers (e.g., someone with Morph who never activates it while anyone is watching, or someone with Remote Perception who doesn't let on that she's spying on anyone) would be a dark star. I wouldn't go that far.</div> </div> </div> </div></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I meant more 'if someone was watching them every second of the day' than just a Nova being sneaky about it. This would include certain Subtle powers, but only those that left no traces, and I think that's still a fair in-universe definition. I mean, if you have someone with Entropy Control manifesting as Subtle Quantum Field and Quantum Deflection, how in the world can observers know they aren't just really lucky?</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1456251-aberrant-examples-and-what-darkstar-novas-would-be-like?p=1456480#post1456480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">But it's true more often than not. Hawkeye and Black Widow don't strike me as terribly sure to Foresight, either. Just because Foresight exists, that doesn't mean that it's any more common than any <i>other</i> Mega-Edge. Assuming that every Mega-Intellect/Mega-Cunning Nova has it is like assuming that every Talent has \u201cThe Bigger They Are\u201d.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">And even some concepts that <i>are</i> suited to Foresight could be better handled as experienced Talents: the Reflective Facet is very similar in feel to Foresight. I could easily see modeling Batman's \u201ccrazy prepared\u201d vibe with five dots of the Reflective Facet. I'd also give him at least three dots of the Destructive Facet, and possibly even a full five (Batman's very big on powering through on sheer grit), and a few dots in the Intuitive Facet (though of the three, that's where he's weakest). Oh, and \u201cThe Bigger They Are\u201d. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> I think I've failed to communicate my intent here. I agree with all this entirely, I was agreeing with you and saying <i>Foresight</i> is not universally applicable, not that your comment isn't.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1456251-aberrant-examples-and-what-darkstar-novas-would-be-like?p=1456480#post1456480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">That's more generous than I would be, surprisingly.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">While neither TC not the TC Adventure manuscript gives a table for experienced characters the way TC Aberrant does, TC \u00c6on does: Experienced characters get an extra 10 points, hardened veterans get 50, hardened veterans get 100, and \u201cProxies or exceptional Talents\u201d (their phrasing) get 150. Considering the phrasing on that last one, I take that chart (p.125) to apply to <i>everyone</i>, save only for Novas who have their own chart that overrides it.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">And yes, that does put non-Novas roughly a hundred experience points behind Novas. But as Mateus Luz says, they have their own benefits. If you're still concerned that they're too far behind, I could see tossing an extra, say, 50 experience their way on general principle; maybe even as much as 100.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">But I'm not sure that they need it. As Mateus Luz says, Talents and Psi-actives don't <i>need</i> as much experience, at least when leaning into their special powers: Gifts cost 4 or 5 xp; Modes cost 6, 8, or 10 xp (for Psions, psiad primaries, and psiad secondaries); Nova Traits mostly cost 12 xp (unless you're willing to take on Transcendence, which has its own price). Facets cost 10 xp; Psi costs 12/15 or 24/30; Quantum costs 16 or 32. And Talents arguably get more from their Facets than Novas get from their Quantum.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> This has not been my experience statting NPCs. A Telekinetic Nova needs to spend most of their staring XP for full coverage but with Quantum 4, Quantum Anima 4 (Technique 4) and Flight, Quantum Attack, Quantum Construct, and Quantum Field at 4 as Techniques, they're just much, much, better at telekinesis than a starting Psychokinetic Psiad or Psion (to the tune of the equivalent of 4 dots in both Telekinesis and Perikinesis, and 1 of Thermokinesis) but with significant Scale as well (and that lovely bit with succeeding on a 7+). The same is true of most areas where there are actually direct correspondences. Some Psion/Psiad stuff is just beyond Novas, it's true, but where there is overlap, Novas tend to win any comparison by a fair bit, IMO.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1456251-aberrant-examples-and-what-darkstar-novas-would-be-like?p=1456480#post1456480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">And with all that in mind, I'd be perfectly happy insisting that a Nova <i>can't</i> spend all of the added xp they get on non-Nova traits. It's rarely an issue, because who in their right mind would play a Nova with no Nova Traits? But I could see insisting that at least 75 to 100 of those experience points should be spend on Nova Traits in one form or another, with the other 50 to 75 prioritizing Nova-related traits such as allegiance or Dormancy over Skills, Skill Tricks, or Edges that anyone can get. And anyone who <i>knows</i> the Nova before and after her Eruption will tend to think of whatever skills come from those points as a sort of Nova Trait, too \u2014 not because the skills can do anything particularly unusual (they can't), but because they came out of nowhere, and are <i>not</i> the result of training: the Nova Erupted, and suddenly could perform at a level that she couldn't before.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">This seems totally reasonable, and indeed very unlikely to come up, as you say.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26949-deadmanwalking","name":"Deadmanwalking","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-10T02:09:09-07:00","id":1456509,"title":"","content":"In terms of 'Dark Star' definitions specifically, the Aberrant book has the following to say:<br /> <br /> -&quot;dark star: a nova whose abilities are subtle enough to 'pass' for baseline.&quot; (Glossary, p. 19)<br /> -&quot;...novas whose enhancements might be mistaken for extraordinary human talents, or who are simply in hiding&quot; (History section, p. 24)<br /> -&quot;...those having some abilities but able to pass in baseline society as highly skilled agents.&quot; (Directive section, p. 141)<br /> -&quot;...have only one or two dots in any given Mega-Attribute, but that's still enough to make them more capable in that area than almost any baseline human, particularly if their underlying Attributes are rating 3 or higher.&quot; ('Mega-Attributes and Stealth Novas' p. 184)<br /> <br /> The term is also mentioned on p. 74 pretty much exclusively for 'novas who are being kept secret' and on p. 107 the term is also implied to contain psychomorphs like Maggie Mercer.<br /> <br /> So yeah, both the 'low Mega-Attributes only' definition and the 'able to pass for baseline' definitions are in print, as is just 'novas not publicly known' (though that last one is in the definite minority). I think the 'subtle enough to pass' definition is most prevalent, but either way, both are definitely correct and clarifying which is being discussed is relevant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26949-deadmanwalking","name":"Deadmanwalking","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-10T14:19:52-07:00","id":1456552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1456251-aberrant-examples-and-what-darkstar-novas-would-be-like?p=1456488#post1456488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know of no portrayal of Batman where he's clearly beyond human. I know of a few where he's maxed out on Inspiration and loaded to the gills with both Gifts and Inspired Super-Science; but he's never <i>clearly</i> beyond human.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing that puts him clearly beyond human is his aggregate abilities. I remember reading an official DC explanation of Batman's capabilities from about 10-20 years ago. He was basically olympic or near-olympic level as a sprinter, marathon runner, swimmer, gymnast, weight lifter, and martial artist. He's also a brilliant polymath and businessman. He manages to fit everything into his daily schedule via short power naps and a specialized high protein diet.<br /> <br /> Being any one of these things is fine, since real people do that stuff. Being a few of those things is also fine, since exceptional people have been known to do that as well. Doing all of it isn't fine, since real humans can't train for all of that at once. A man with a weight lifter's build is flat out the wrong body type to properly excel at several of those other athletic tasks., so at least some &quot;normal&quot; humans in the DC universe can apparently train themselves to an impossible degree of competence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-10T14:47:32-07:00","id":1456555,"title":"","content":"That is the point. Batman is not the only one in DC universe that excel in that many things, many of the villains are considered humans but are impossibly capable in too many things simultaneously.<br /> <br /> Cat woman was a regular woman that had a mental breakdown and become amazingly agile and good with a whip in a level not seen since westerns.<br /> <br /> Harlequin was a psychologist that become inumanos strong and resistant to her body size, just because she was turned insane by one of her patients.<br /> <br /> Penguin is a genius with a deformed body that become a the kingpin of Gotham (by the way, the most normal person of them all).<br /> <br /> Riddler was an regular employee with above average intellect and after a mental breakdown become a super genius capable of create traps and weird riddles that drive people crazy.<br /> <br /> Scarecrow was a psychologist that after a mental breakdown become the ultimate expert in causing fear in people while are capable of run for ever without tiring and not even seam breathless.<br /> <br /> Those mental breakdown are amazing to the body\u2026","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-10T20:16:05-07:00","id":1456574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shepherdboi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1456251-aberrant-examples-and-what-darkstar-novas-would-be-like?p=1456552#post1456552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing that puts him clearly beyond human is his aggregate abilities. I remember reading an official DC explanation of Batman's capabilities from about 10-20 years ago. He was basically olympic or near-olympic level as a sprinter, marathon runner, swimmer, gymnast, weight lifter, and martial artist. He's also a brilliant polymath and businessman. He manages to fit everything into his daily schedule via short power naps and a specialized high protein diet.<br /> <br /> Being any one of these things is fine, since real people do that stuff. Being a few of those things is also fine, since exceptional people have been known to do that as well. Doing all of it isn't fine, since real humans can't train for all of that at once. A man with a weight lifter's build is flat out the wrong body type to properly excel at several of those other athletic tasks., so at least some &quot;normal&quot; humans in the DC universe can apparently train themselves to an impossible degree of competence.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is just PCs of any sort with enough xp, though. In real life, nobody actually has the equivalent of Mit 5, Dex 5, Stm 5, but Batman (as a baseline, if you made him that way) would have exactly that...as can your PC if that's how you spend your xp. It's terribly unrealistic, but fits the genre convention of highly competent protagonists that Trinity Continuum is following. <br /> <br /> It's certainly doable even at less stats as a Talent, simply by using Extraordinary Effort as necessary (Mit 3, Athletics 3, and Extraordinary Effort are mechanically better than Mit 5, Athletics 5). Really, a Talent can thus duplicate every Mega-Attribute at 1 in terms of their maximum potential, if only briefly. That's enough for Batman, at least in theory (and in combination with The Bigger They Are for fighting superhumans). <br /> <br /> Personally, I still think he generally works better as a Nova (Mega-Intellect, Mega-Cunning, and Mega-Composure in excess of 1 are all very on-theme, as is a bit of Q-Tech), but it depends on what version of Batman you're doing, and he's also viable as a Talent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26949-deadmanwalking","name":"Deadmanwalking","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-11T03:07:23-07:00","id":1456587,"title":"","content":"Batman can also have some skill tricks to increase scale on specific situations, and with enough skill tricks it\u2019s possible to cover a large spectrum of actions","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-11T03:48:59-07:00","id":1456589,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1456251-aberrant-examples-and-what-darkstar-novas-would-be-like?p=1456587#post1456587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Batman can also have some skill tricks to increase scale on specific situations, and with enough skill tricks it\u2019s possible to cover a large spectrum of actions</div> </div> </div> </div>Quick note: in the rules as written, there's a hard limit as to how many Skill Tricks you can have: no more than three per Skill, and then only if you have the Skill at five dots. IMHO, though, Talents should be an exception to that, either by loosening up the cap a bit (e.g., they can have twice as many Skill Tricks then a baseline for their skill level) or by removing it entirely. Or maybe a mix of the two: for instance, let them have two Skill Tricks at the third dot, four at the fourth, and as many as they want at the fifth. <br /> <br /> Also: if Batman has The Bigger They Are, then there are a number of cases where someone might mistakenly think that he's somehow got Scale (because \u201cyou'd <i>have</i> to have Scale to deal with <i>that</i>\u201d) when in fact he's merely ignoring the <i>opposition's</i> Scale. <br /> <br /> And finally, I wouldn't give Batman maxed out Might, or Manipulation, for that matter. In the first case, he's regularly shown to be at a disadvantage strength-wise against muscle-bound goons. And he's not really the type who manipulates people, save for a handful of cases that can readily be handled with Skill Tricks and/or Gifts; he tends to rely more on Presence in his social interactions. He's still better than average in these \u201cweak spots\u201d of his attribute spread; but I could easily see him \u201conly\u201d having three dots in each.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-11T04:25:35-07:00","id":1456593,"title":"","content":"Skill Tricks have another problem, besides what Dataweaver pointed: they are fueled by Momentum. This makes them a) more rarely used than we normally think they would and b) bound to other player's permission to be used.<br /> <br /> There are three rules about Skill Tricks that I think the Core should have addressed, but as far as I know, didn't:<br /> 1) Create some mechanism for Talents to use Skill Tricks by spending a personal resource.<br /> 2) Create some mechanism for Talents to have more Skill Tricks than currently allowed (as Dataweaver pointed), and/or emulate Skill Tricks (similar to Aberrants Prodigy Mega-Edge).<br /> <br /> 3) Clarify the issue about NPCs and Skill Tricks: do they have them? If so, how they use them, since they spend Momentum? I house-ruled this one like this: whenever an NPC is in the verge of using a Skill Trick, the Storyguide decides if doing so is something &quot;pro-troupe&quot; or &quot;against-the-troupe&quot;. If it's pro-troupe, the players pay with their Momentum (exactly as if it was a PC); if it's against-the-troupe, then any Momentum the NPC &quot;spends&quot; is actually added to the Players Momentum Pool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1001-timecrafter","name":"Timecrafter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1001_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-11T04:48:46-07:00","id":1456594,"title":"","content":"Yes; Momentum being an inherently shared resource has proven problematic for our group. Instead, we treated as a shareable resource: each character has his or her own Momentum Pool, but any player can freely donate his or her character's Momentum points to anyone's, for any reason. Rather than there being a \u201cgroup veto\u201d on spending Momentum, everyone can spend the Momentum that he or she has earned freely; and that includes spending it on what <i>someone else</i> is trying to do. It solves a lot of problems for us. <br /> <br /> That's why I didn't really address the first and third points Timecrafter mentioned: at my table, they're non-issues.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-11T06:02:38-07:00","id":1456595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1456251-aberrant-examples-and-what-darkstar-novas-would-be-like?p=1456589#post1456589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And finally, I wouldn't give Batman maxed out Might, or Manipulation, for that matter. In the first case, he's regularly shown to be at a disadvantage strength-wise against muscle-bound goons. And he's not really the type who manipulates people, save for a handful of cases that can readily be handled with Skill Tricks and/or Gifts; he tends to rely more on Presence in his social interactions. He's still better than average in these \u201cweak spots\u201d of his attribute spread; but I could easily see him \u201conly\u201d having three dots in each.</div> </div> </div> </div>Batman is, when he decides to be, a really superb liar which is why I'd give the Nova version some Mega-Manipulation (since Mega-Cunning won't help), but the Talent version could likely manage that with Cunning instead, causing less need for Manipulation. I also basically agree on the Might.<br /> <br /> If I were to define Batman's Attributes as a Talent it'd probably be something like Int 5, Cun 5, Res 5, Mit 3, Dex 5, Stm 4, Pre 4, Man 3, Com 5 with maybe Composure or Intellect getting superior Trait for a 6. Then lots of points of Skills and Edges and several Enhanced Edges (well, Loaded and Indomitable anyway). <br /> <br /> The Nova version probably needs less xp to represent him properly, but likely still has at least a 3 in every Attribute (possibly not Might...with Mega-Might 1 and good Athletics a Might of 2 might be sufficient) and at least 1 in every Mega-Attribute (more like 3+ in Mega-Intellect, Mega-Cunning, and Mega-Composure).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26949-deadmanwalking","name":"Deadmanwalking","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-11T07:14:41-07:00","id":1456597,"title":"","content":"Don't forget the Gifts. That's why I'm not terribly concerned with giving him a full Manipulation of five: a Gift that gives him a targeted ability to lie covers the times that he is really good at deceiving people, such as his whole playboy routine as Bruce Wayne.<br /> <br /> And, of course, \u201cwhen he needs to\u201d, he can always spend Inspiration on a Destructive, Intuitive, or Reflective Action (to increase the dice pool) or on Extraordinary Effort (to boost his effective Scale), or on Talented Defense (to boost his defense). While it's true that his weakest Facet is Intuitive, and that that's what he'd most likely need to be a superb liar when the situation demands, I also think that for \u201cgod-mode Batman\u201d as a Talent, his weakest Facet would be a 3.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-11T09:14:00-07:00","id":1456608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1456251-aberrant-examples-and-what-darkstar-novas-would-be-like?p=1456594#post1456594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes; Momentum being an inherently shared resource has proven problematic for our group. Instead, we treated as a shareable resource: each character has his or her own Momentum Pool, but any player can freely donate his or her character's Momentum points to anyone's, for any reason. Rather than there being a \u201cgroup veto\u201d on spending Momentum, everyone can spend the Momentum that he or she has earned freely; and that includes spending it on what <i>someone else</i> is trying to do. It solves a lot of problems for us. <br /> <br /> That's why I didn't really address the first and third points Timecrafter mentioned: at my table, they're non-issues.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really like this fix for Momentum","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4178-stanlemon","name":"stanlemon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-12T17:19:03-07:00","id":1456721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1456251-aberrant-examples-and-what-darkstar-novas-would-be-like?p=1456589#post1456589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And finally, I wouldn't give Batman maxed out Might, or Manipulation, for that matter. In the first case, he's regularly shown to be at a disadvantage strength-wise against muscle-bound goons. And he's not really the type who manipulates people, save for a handful of cases that can readily be handled with Skill Tricks and/or Gifts; he tends to rely more on Presence in his social interactions. He's still better than average in these \u201cweak spots\u201d of his attribute spread; but I could easily see him \u201conly\u201d having three dots in each.</div> </div> </div> </div>Batman is highly manipulative (with numerous storylines based around this tendancy) and built like a linebacker (6'2&quot; and 210 lbs.). According to a quick google of an article on the Livestrong website, this puts him 10 lbs. above his ideal weight lifter weight. He may not have Might 5, but he's certainly not Might 3.<br /> <br /> If I had to stat up his Attributes, I'd probably go with something along the lines of:<br /> <br /> Physical:<br /> -Might: 4-5<br /> -Dexterity: 3-4 (above average to exceptional, boosted by Skills and Edges. Nightwing is Dex 5. Catwoman is probably Dex 6)<br /> -Stamina 5-6 (necessary for the extra health box, and to maintain his absurd schedule)<br /> <br /> Mental:<br /> -Intellect: 4-5<br /> -Cunning: 4-5<br /> -Resolve: 4-6 (endured being repeatedly tortured to death by a godlike Joker, then turned the tables on him)<br /> <br /> Social:<br /> -Presence: 4-5 (super intimidating, and draws sidekicks like moths despite being a curmudgeon)<br /> -Manipulation: 4-5 (constantly plots against allies &amp; lives a highly public cover life as Bruce Wayne)<br /> -Composure: 4-5 (virtually unfazeable)<br /> <br /> He'd also have at least 3 dots in every single Skill, with lots of Skill Tricks and Edges.<br /> <br /> edit:<br /> <br /> For extra Bat-Cheese, Batman probably has Technology 5 with a specialization in Bat-Gear. This gives him +3 enhancement to Aim rolls with Batarangs and Bat-Grapple guns.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25506,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","user":"Shepherdboi","date":". 08-12-2021, 08:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-12T17:29:15-07:00","id":1456722,"title":"","content":"Manipulation is not about scheming; that's covered by Intellect. The Bruce Wayne thing is more a matter of being exceptionally skilled at maintaining an alternate persona; that's more of a skill thing than an attribute thing. What Manipulation covers is the ability to get others to do what you want them to <i>without</i> the shock and awe approach that Presence represents. And frankly, Batman's not very good at that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-13T11:59:35-07:00","id":1456773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1456251-aberrant-examples-and-what-darkstar-novas-would-be-like?p=1456722#post1456722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Manipulation is not about scheming; that's covered by Intellect. The Bruce Wayne thing is more a matter of being exceptionally skilled at maintaining an alternate persona; that's more of a skill thing than an attribute thing. What Manipulation covers is the ability to get others to do what you want them to <i>without</i> the shock and awe approach that Presence represents. And frankly, Batman's not very good at that.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> But Manipulation is also about how good you are at reading other people and he is quite good at that.<br /> <br /> One reason I wouldn't model comics Batman as a Talent is that to do so all his Attributes would have to be near peak. I feel a Darkstar would be better at that with Scale boost plus to cover some of his other crazy things he does. In fact I like this conversation because it shows just how blurry the line in universe can be between Talents and some low level Novas","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4178-stanlemon","name":"stanlemon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-13T12:57:49-07:00","id":1456778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>stanlemon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1456251-aberrant-examples-and-what-darkstar-novas-would-be-like?p=1456773#post1456773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But Manipulation is also about how good you are at reading other people and he is quite good at that.</div> </div> </div> </div> Not really, no: to the extent that he's good at reading people, it's more a matter of Cunning, and/or a Gift. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>stanlemon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1456251-aberrant-examples-and-what-darkstar-novas-would-be-like?p=1456773#post1456773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One reason I wouldn't model comics Batman as a Talent is that to do so all his Attributes would have to be near peak.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you may be underestimating how much Inspiration can make a Talent larger than life. It's not just, or even primarily, Dramatic Editing: the facet related actions, the extraordinary effort, and The Talented defense allow a talent who operate as a highly competent individual most of the time to boost his effectiveness to borderline superhuman level when it counts. And that's what you generally see with Batman: he normally operates at a level that is exceptionally capable but not overwhelmingly so; but when it really matters, he can take it up a notch. I think you may be conflating Batman when he takes it up a notch (i.e., when Inspiration is involved) with Batman as he is the rest of the time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-14T15:35:20-07:00","id":1456835,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1456251-aberrant-examples-and-what-darkstar-novas-would-be-like?p=1456778#post1456778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Not really, no: to the extent that he's good at reading people, it's more a matter of Cunning, and/or a Gift.</div> </div> </div> </div>Um this quote from the book seems pretty unambiguous that Manipulation is used to read people<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Manipulation measures a character\u2019s ability to fine tune their social skills and to<b> analyze social cues</b>. The \u201chard sell\u201d requires a high Presence. Intricate trickery requires a high Manipulation. Characters who require a high Manipulation are politicians, spies, and con artists. Low Manipulation characters lack subtlety or empathy. <b>High Manipulation characters are able to read people well. </b>Manipulation can be used for: managing people, lying convincingly, sleight of hand, <b>noticing social cues</b>, seduction, or subduing a hostile animal. </div> </div> </div>As for this<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think you may be underestimating how much Inspiration can make a Talent larger than life. It's not just, or even primarily, Dramatic Editing: the facet related actions, the extraordinary effort, and The Talented defense allow a talent who operate as a highly competent individual most of the time to boost his effectiveness to borderline superhuman level when it counts. And that's what you generally see with Batman: he normally operates at a level that is exceptionally capable but not overwhelmingly so; but when it really matters, he can take it up a notch. I think you may be conflating Batman when he takes it up a notch (i.e., when Inspiration is involved) with Batman as he is the rest of the time. </div> </div> </div>While it is possible, this is why I said Batman is hard to pin down Darkstar or Talent. In his own comics he often is as you say, but any time he's with the Justice League his base operating level is what would be considered taking it up a notch in many of his own comics. Taking the whole of his characterizations in DC comics is why I would rank him as a Darkstar Nova over a Talent<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4178-stanlemon","name":"stanlemon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-15T05:01:01-07:00","id":1456869,"title":"","content":"Nobody is saying that Manipulation doesn't let you read people, but many actions fall under multiple stats in this system. Sure Manipulation covers reading people, but Cunning also says that 'notice details quickly' and includes 'understand a political situation', 'act' and 'con' in its list of actions you can do with it (and conning absolutely involves getting a read on people). Similarly, Composure specifically notes that it covers 'recognizing when one is being lied to or otherwise deceived'. Under 'Empathy', the actual skill for reading people, telling when someone is lying to you is listed as Composure while 'reading what a business rival wants' is Cunning + Empathy. Only playing good cop in an interrogation is listed as Manipulation.<br /> <br /> None of which is to say you can't do some of those things with Manipulation as well, but Cunning and Composure really do cover most of it.<br /> <br /> Now, if talking about Batman as a Nova specifically, this is a lot less true, because Mega-Cunning and Mega-Composure are pretty divergent from Mega-Manipulation in what they do, and Batman probably would need Mega-Manipulation's Scale increase...but as a Talent, he can raise Scale on Cunning or Composure just as easily as he can Manipulation, and thus can get by just fine with Manipulation 3 or so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26949-deadmanwalking","user":"Deadmanwalking","date":". 08-15-2021, 08:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26949-deadmanwalking","name":"Deadmanwalking","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-15T11:00:01-07:00","id":1456884,"title":"","content":"They way Cunning is described in the books presents it at least to me as understanding how things are going on in the moment. Whereas Manipulation is what is important for understanding why someone is doing it and how to use that information. Take Batman's infamous plans to take out the Justice League members should they ever turn, that would require decent understanding of their motives to...well...manipulate them to make them work.<br /> <br /> Sure Cunning works for the 'act' and 'con' but that has more to do with thinking on your feet and quickly which is one of the two main focuses of Cunning.<br /> <br /> Edit: Back to the topic of if Batman has high Manipulation or not, regardless of what is used to read people. I'd still argue that he does have at minimum above average Manipulation as he manages to maintain his high profile secret identity as Bruce Wayne and he often wins his battles by tricking his opponents.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4178,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4178-stanlemon","user":"stanlemon","date":". 08-15-2021, 02:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4178-stanlemon","name":"stanlemon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-15T12:07:51-07:00","id":1456894,"title":"","content":"Above average, sure. I was mainly arguing against it having to be maxed out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}